{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add an `mcp` autodeploy target to `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` implementing the ADR 0079\namendment's blue-green pointer-swap, so on-box `rebar-mcp` tracks `origin/main` without killing an\nin-flight certified op. Scope: the MCP deploy path only (service/edge = esok, secrets =\navians); no new timer (`rebar-autodeploy.timer`→`.service` runs `autodeploy.sh`).\n\n## Approach (blue-green, ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur / 0079 amendment)\nModel on the LOCAL `origin/main` updater (`sticky-genetic-narwhal`): immutable release + atomic\npointer swap + retire-when-idle, NOT the review-bot stop-and-drain. On an MCP source change:\n1. Build + tag immutable `compose-mcp:<target-sha>` (`docker compose build mcp`).\n2. **Memory pre-check BEFORE the 2x overlap** (t4g.large 8 GiB): read `MemAvailable`\n   (`/proc/meminfo`, MB); `< MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` (default 1024) ABORTS — emit `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT`,\n   record backoff, start NO second container. Unreadable fails OPEN; `MCP_MEM_AVAILABLE_MB` overrides.\n3. Start a NEW container alongside old via **`docker run -d`** (see Run mechanism) on the OTHER A/B\n   host port; one-in/one-out, never N.\n4. Health-check the NEW `/health` 200 within `MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT` (default 120). On failure:\n   `docker rm -f` new, leave OLD include UNCHANGED (rollback = do nothing), `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`\n   reason `mcp-unhealthy`, backoff, exit 1 → next tick retries.\n5. **Atomically flip the nginx `/mcp/` upstream**: back up the include, write\n   `server 127.0.0.1:<newport>;` to a temp file, `mv` over `/etc/nginx/mcp-upstream.conf`,\n   `nginx -t`, `nginx -s reload`. If `nginx -t`/reload fails: RESTORE the backup, `docker rm -f`\n   new, record backoff, exit 1. Deploy is DONE at a successful reload; never waited on/killed an op.\n6. **Retire the OLD container off the critical path**, gated by a \"still serving?\" check on its\n   `/health` `in_flight` gauge. Retain newest `MCP_RELEASES_KEEP` (default 1); remove older ones\n   ONLY when idle; NEVER kill `in_flight>0`. If the managed count exceeds `MCP_RELEASES_CAP`\n   (default 3) because busy containers can't be reclaimed, emit `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP`\n   instead of killing a live one or growing unbounded.\n\nWhy: eliminates bug 7b4a (never-idle shared MCP can't satisfy a gauge-gated drain bound);\ndecoupling retire from deploy means it never blocks/kills, and a killed op is client-visible +\nidempotent so retire is safe.\n\n## Run mechanism + the original compose container (bootstrap)\n`docker compose up mcp` pins `8091` and would recreate/collide, so it CANNOT run the parallel\ncontainer. The NEW container starts via **`docker run -d`** from `compose-mcp:<sha>` (helper\n`mcp_run_new`) reproducing the compose `mcp:` service on the alternate HOST port\n`-p 127.0.0.1:<newport>:8091` (container port stays 8091; host port alternates\n`MCP_PORT_A=8091`↔`MCP_PORT_B=8092`): `--env-file \"$COMPOSE_DIR/.env\"`, the same `REBAR_MCP_*` +\n`REBAR_OPCERT_*` env, the two `:ro` secret bind-mounts, `--restart always`, `--stop-timeout 1260`\n— a comment marks these MIRRORING `docker-compose.yml`'s `mcp:`. The live port is read from the include; the new takes the other.\n\nAt boot `compose-up.sh` `docker compose up -d`s the whole stack, so the ORIGINAL container is\n`compose-mcp-1` on 8091 (seed include→8091). The managed MCP set the sweep/cap count over =\nnames matching `MCP_CONTAINER_PREFIX` (`rebar-mcp`) OR `MCP_COMPOSE_CONTAINER` (default\n`compose-mcp-1`). So the first deploy's OLD backend is `compose-mcp-1`, adopted into\nretire-when-idle by the same liveness gate (autodeploy never runs `docker compose up mcp`); cap\naccounting counts the union. On reboot compose recreates `compose-mcp-1` and\nDocker restarts the `--restart always` live container; the sweep reclaims the redundant idle one.\n\n## Retire-when-idle re-trigger\n`autodeploy.sh` exits early when up-to-date, so run a lightweight `mcp_retire_sweep` on the no-op\ntick (like `reclaim_under_pressure`): reclaim idle old containers + fire the over-cap alert, no\nbuild/flip — retirement re-triggers once a container goes idle.\n\n## Change detection + blast radius\n`MCP_PATHS='src/rebar infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp infra/compose/docker-compose.yml uv.lock pyproject.toml'`\n— the canonical set esok committed in the `mcp:` compose-comment contract. Diffed\n`deployed..target` it triggers ONLY `mcp`. Since `src/rebar` and `docker-compose.yml` are shared\nwith `BOT_PATHS`, a shared change triggers BOTH targets, each in its own independent `if changed`\nblock. `gerrit` is never touched (add a before/after gerrit-id assert). `flock` still serializes.\n\n## Failure interaction with deployed-sha + backoff\nThe `mcp` branch failure is FATAL like the `review-bot` branch (`record_backoff_failure` +\n`exit 1`), so the footer advancing `deployed-sha` is not reached. For a shared change the\nreview-bot block runs first; if it succeeds but mcp fails, `deployed-sha` does not advance and BOTH\nretry next tick (review-bot rebuild is idempotent) — a failed mcp deploy is always retried.\n\n## Alerting (marker → observability → CloudWatch → SNS; NO direct SNS publish)\nautodeploy.sh has no `sns:Publish` path and must not gain one. The alert is emitted like every\nexisting autodeploy alert: a countable `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_* {json}` → `observability.sh` greps\nthe journal via `publish_autodeploy_marker_delta` into a dimensionless `rebar/host` metric → a\nterraform `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` routes it to `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`. Adds tokens\n`AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` + `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT`; two `publish_autodeploy_marker_delta`\ncalls (+ offset files) publishing `rebar/host:mcp_retire_cap` + `rebar/host:mcp_mem_abort`; two\n`aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm` resources mirroring `monitoring_autodeploy.tf`'s dimensionless\n900s/2-of-4/Sum>0/notBreaching shape. Both tokens are distinct from `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`.\n\n## Portability (`project.portability`)\nTrigger is the on-box systemd/launchd timer polling the git mirror — operation-linked, not a CI\nprovider. Drain/flip/retire run in-process; works with any/no CI.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tier: **real subprocess/bash integration, temp git repos + fake docker/nginx**. Tests stub\n  the box binaries onto PATH and run the REAL `autodeploy.sh`, in `tests/scripts/`. Oracles:\n  - Change detection (REAL temp git repo, two commits): an MCP-only change (touch\n    `Dockerfile.mcp`) triggers `mcp` and NO review-bot/gerrit rebuild; a review-bot-only change\n    (touch `Dockerfile.reviewbot`, not in `MCP_PATHS`) does the inverse; a shared `src/rebar`\n    change triggers BOTH independently — via the docker call log.\n  - Cutover order start-new → health → flip → retire (recorded docker/nginx/curl log); the deploy\n    returns success WITHOUT waiting on `in_flight` (with `in_flight>0` on OLD it still flips to the\n    new port and exits 0).\n  - Retire honors liveness: an OLD container with `in_flight>0` is NOT killed (no `docker rm` of\n    it); over `MCP_RELEASES_CAP` the `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP` marker is emitted, no live\n    container deleted.\n  - Memory pre-check: `MCP_MEM_AVAILABLE_MB < MCP_MEM_MIN_MB` ABORTS — no second container started,\n    `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT` emitted, backoff recorded, include unchanged.\n  - Health-check failure leaves the OLD include byte-identical (`AUTODEPLOY_ERROR` reason\n    `mcp-unhealthy`, backoff recorded, `deployed-sha` not advanced); a retry on the next healthy\n    tick flips the include.\n  - `gerrit` container id UNCHANGED across an mcp deploy (blast-radius oracle).\n- [ ] observability.sh publishes `rebar/host:mcp_retire_cap` + `rebar/host:mcp_mem_abort` from the\n  two markers. Two terraform CloudWatch alarms route the two metrics to `aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn`,\n  mirroring `monitoring_autodeploy.tf`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nAdditive (new `if changed \"$MCP_PATHS\"` block + no-op sweep); other targets unchanged (existing\nautodeploy tests stay green). ADRs 0079/0104 document it. Rollback = revert the additions.\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur, cibophobic-holohedral-esok."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787625318505816001,"uuid":"b1e7f33c-d793-4ae1-b6dd-b4eb68606dae"}